{"lines": ["Numbers stations are shortwave broadcasts of formatted numbers, addressed to intelligence officers working in foreign countries.", "Most use synthetic speech, though some use Morse code or digital modes.", "Some keep a set schedule. Others come on at irregular times.", "The most famous was the Lincolnshire Poacher, a British station.", "It opened with bars from an English folk song, then a woman's voice read groups of five numbers, like zero, two, five, eight, eight.", "Amateur enthusiasts traced it to the RAF base at Akrotiri, in Cyprus.", "Its last recorded transmission came on July 2nd, 2008.", "No government has confirmed that numbers stations exist.", "Those were signals with a sender. The next one may have no sender at all."], "words": [["Numbers", 0.0, 0.26], ["stations", 0.26, 0.58], ["are", 0.58, 1.24], ["shortwave", 1.24, 1.74], ["broadcasts", 1.74, 2.3], ["of", 2.3, 2.82], ["formatted", 2.82, 3.22], ["numbers,", 3.22, 3.9], ["addressed", 4.04, 4.56], ["to", 4.56, 4.94], ["intelligence", 4.94, 5.36], ["officers", 5.36, 5.94], ["working", 5.94, 6.42], ["in", 6.42, 6.78], ["foreign", 6.78, 7.04], ["countries.", 7.04, 7.58], ["Most", 8.16, 8.38], ["use", 8.38, 8.58], ["synthetic", 8.58, 9.04], ["speech,", 9.04, 9.5], ["though", 9.94, 10.16], ["some", 10.16, 10.38], ["use", 10.38, 10.6], ["Morse", 10.6, 10.82], ["code", 10.82, 11.2], ["or", 11.2, 11.7], ["digital", 11.7, 12.0], ["modes.", 12.0, 12.38], ["Some", 13.2, 13.26], ["keep", 13.26, 13.46], ["a", 13.46, 13.6], ["set", 13.6, 13.82], ["schedule.", 13.82, 14.18], ["Others", 14.78, 15.14], ["come", 15.14, 15.4], ["on", 15.4, 15.66], ["at", 15.66, 15.88], ["irregular", 15.88, 16.04], ["times.", 16.04, 16.72], ["The", 17.34, 17.42], ["most", 17.42, 17.58], ["famous", 17.58, 18.02], ["was", 18.02, 18.44], ["the", 18.44, 18.6], ["Lincolnshire", 18.6, 19.16], ["Poacher,", 19.16, 19.64], ["a", 19.92, 20.08], ["British", 20.08, 20.28], ["station.", 20.28, 20.62], ["It", 21.24, 21.4], ["opened", 21.4, 